<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Norway</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Norwegian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Norway is a Scandinavian country on the western side of the Scandinavian Peninsula, united with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> for much of the early modern period. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a> won Norwegian provinces including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trondheim">Trondheim</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohuslan">Bohuslän</a> from Denmark-Norway in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-roskilde">Treaty of Roskilde</a> in 1658. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII of Sweden</a> was killed in 1718 while invading Norway, at the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-fredriksten">Fredriksten</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/norway.jpg" alt="Norway" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Fredrik Meltzer Vector: Gutten på Hemsen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Norway.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
